{
  "dom_id": "step-q84987",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "How many made-up $4$-letter words can be made using $21$ consonants, where each consonant cannot appear in the word more than once?",
  "worked_solution": "The number of permutations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $21$ consonants, so $n=21.$ We want to select $4$ of those consonants to make-up a $4$-letter word, so we have $r=4.$\n\nTherefore, the number of different made-up words is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{21}{P}_{4} & =\\frac{21!}{(21-4)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{21!}{17!} \\\\  & =\\frac{21\\cdot 20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18\\cdot \\cancel{17!}}{\\cancel{17!}} \\\\  & =21\\cdot 20\\cdot 19\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =143\\,640.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
